  os: "Debian GNU/Linux 11 (Bullseye) 64-bit"
  domain: "domain_1"

analysis:
  root_cause: >
    Not applicable — requirement change, not a defect.
  technical_notes: >
    _get_shift_cue()'s return tuple (border_colour, border_width,
    flash_centre, centre_colour) is only ever destructured for
    border_colour and centre_colour by its one caller in
    _draw_radial_mode(); border_width and the flash_centre flag are
    already discarded there. Once border_colour's only consumer
    (_draw_shift_border) is removed, and the flash is not being
    relocated, _get_shift_cue() has no remaining reason to exist:
    _draw_radial_mode() can read palette.band_centres[active_band]
    directly, exactly as _get_shift_cue() did for its own non-flashing
    branches.
